# `npm version` tags as agent-v<version>, not npm's default v<version>.
#
# This is load-bearing, not cosmetic. The release workflow triggers on
# `agent-v*` tags; with npm's default prefix, `npm version patch` bumps
# package.json and pushes a `v0.2.1` tag that matches nothing, so the release
# silently never runs. The version having moved makes it look like it did.
#
# The agent-v prefix also keeps agent releases distinguishable from any future
# tags on the server side of this repo.
tag-version-prefix=agent-v
